CAT = "sgvlInclusive"; SEG = "INC"
# Paper A: passengers with disabilities, older passengers and children.
Q = [
("A wheelchair user books your car and uses a folding wheelchair. What should you do?",
 "Ask how they want help, then stow it", ["Lift them into the car without asking first", "Tell them to fold it themselves", "Refuse, as wheelchairs damage cars"],
 "Ask first: the passenger knows how best to transfer and how the chair folds. Then store it carefully in the boot."),
("You see a road sign showing white walking sticks. What should you do?",
 "Slow down; stop for blind people crossing", ["Sound the horn to warn the pedestrians ahead", "Keep your speed, as it marks a footpath only", "Stop only if a police officer is present"],
 "The white walking sticks sign warns of blind pedestrians. Slow down and stop if necessary to give way to blind people crossing the road."),
("You arrive for a booked passenger who is blind and waiting at the kerb. What should you do first?",
 "Say who you are and name the booking", ["Sound the horn twice and wait", "Flash the headlights to signal", "Wait in the car until they find you"],
 "A horn or headlights mean nothing to someone who cannot see you. Walk over, introduce yourself, confirm the booking and offer your arm to the door."),
("You arrive at the destination of a passenger who cannot see. What should you do?",
 "Say you have arrived and where", ["Stop and wait in silence for them to move", "Unlock the doors without speaking", "Leave the meter running"],
 "Tell the passenger you have arrived, which side to get out on and what is around, such as a step or a kerb."),
("A passenger who is deaf gives you a written address. How should you communicate?",
 "Face them; use writing or a phone", ["Shout so that they can hear you", "Talk while looking ahead at the road", "Ignore them and drive off"],
 "Many deaf people lip-read. Face them, speak clearly or type on a phone, and confirm the destination in writing."),
("An elderly passenger takes a long time to get into the car. What should you do?",
 "Be patient and offer help", ["Sound the horn to hurry them up", "Start the meter early", "Drive off before they settle in"],
 "Older passengers may need time and a steady hand. Patience is part of the service and keeps them safe."),
("A passenger with dementia seems confused about where they live. What should you do?",
 "Stay calm and contact a carer or police", ["Drop them at any nearby HDB block", "Tell them to get out and walk home", "Drive around until they remember"],
 "Look for a contact card or ask gently. If you cannot find a safe destination, contact a family member, carer or the police."),
("Which seat is usually easiest for a passenger with limited mobility?",
 "The front seat, pushed back", ["The middle rear seat", "The rear seat directly behind you", "Any seat, it makes no difference"],
 "A front seat moved back gives most room to swing the legs in, but always ask the passenger what works for them."),
("A private hire car passenger is travelling with a child shorter than 1.35 m. What must the car provide?",
 "A booster seat or child restraint", ["Nothing, as long as the trip is short", "An adult seat belt only", "A cushion placed under the child"],
 "Private hire cars must provide booster seats or child restraints for passengers below 1.35 m in height, whatever their age."),
("When must a private hire car provide a child restraint for a passenger under 1.35 m?",
 "Whatever the child's age", ["Only for children under 3", "Only on expressway trips", "Only if the parent asks"],
 "The rule for private hire cars is set by height, not age: anyone under 1.35 m needs a booster seat or child restraint."),
("A passenger uses a walking frame. What helps them most?",
 "Close to the kerb, on level ground", ["In the middle lane at the lights", "On a slope, to save time", "Far from the entrance"],
 "A level stop close to the kerb and entrance makes getting in and out much safer."),
("A passenger with an intellectual disability is travelling alone. How should you speak to them?",
 "Plainly, as you would any adult", ["As you would speak to a small child", "Only to their carer, by phone", "Loudly and slowly in every word"],
 "Use clear, simple words and treat the passenger with the same respect as any adult."),
("A wheelchair user asks if your vehicle can take their motorised chair. It cannot. What should you do?",
 "Explain and help book a suitable car", ["Try to force it into the boot anyway", "Tell them they should not travel", "Leave without explaining"],
 "Heavy motorised chairs need a wheelchair-accessible vehicle. Be honest and help them find one."),
("A pregnant passenger asks you to drive gently. What should you do?",
 "Drive smoothly, braking gently", ["Take the fastest route at higher speed", "Ask her to move to the front seat", "Turn on the hazard lights"],
 "Smooth acceleration and braking make the ride more comfortable and safe."),
("A passenger has a hidden disability and asks for quiet. What should you do?",
 "Respect it without questions", ["Ask them to prove the condition first", "Keep the radio on loud", "Charge extra for the special request"],
 "Not every disability can be seen. Respect reasonable requests without asking for explanations."),
("An older passenger pays with cash and counts slowly. What is good practice?",
 "Wait and count the change back", ["Take the purse and count it yourself", "Round the fare up for the time taken", "Rush them out of the car"],
 "Never handle a passenger's purse. Wait, count the change back clearly and thank them."),
("A child aged about ten is alone, waiting to be picked up by a booked car. What should you check?",
 "That an adult expects them", ["Nothing, children travel the same as adults", "That the child can pay with cash", "That the child sits in the front seat"],
 "Make sure the booking is genuine and that an adult at the destination is expected. If something seems wrong, contact the operator."),
("A passenger with a stoma bag asks you to avoid sudden bumps. What should you do?",
 "Drive smoothly on an even route", ["Say it is not your problem to solve", "Drive faster to finish the trip sooner", "Refuse the booking"],
 "Small adjustments in driving style help passengers with medical needs travel in comfort."),
("A passenger uses sign language with a friend. What should you avoid?",
 "Staring or commenting on it", ["Waiting for them to finish", "Confirming the address in writing", "Driving smoothly"],
 "Treat sign language like any other private conversation."),
("A passenger who is blind wants to pay by card. How can you help?",
 "Say the amount; guide them to the reader", ["Take their card and ask for their PIN", "Ask a bystander to pay for them", "Insist on cash only"],
 "Say the fare clearly and guide their hand to the card reader. Never ask for their PIN."),
]
